Native suite selection: Upstream PG18 basic schedule and isolation schedule are retained and passed to native PG_REGRESS/PG_ISOLATION_REGRESS.
Expected output/test inputs are copied byte-for-byte; no custom SQL assertions or edited expected files are included.
Requirements / limitations:
  Full PG18 native basic regression schedule plus upstream isolation schedule. Remote server must have documentdb_core, documentdb, pg_cron, vector, postgis, and tsm_system_rows available, loadable, and configured; native regression config expects shared_preload_libraries=pg_documentdb_core,pg_documentdb,pg_cron and other PGDG test GUCs. It uses existing server mode because upstream package installcheck is intended for an installed cluster.
PGDG autopkgtest itself only creates the extension through pg_buildext; source regressions are broader and require the exact upstream PG18 schedule plus server preload/configuration.
The upstream Makefile's additional static check-test-output validation target is not run; it is not part of PGDG installcheck.
